## Methodological Warning
**IMPORTANT:** Associations observed in the dataset should not be interpreted as causal relationships. This is a cross-sectional study.

## Rubric
| Criterion | Excellent | Adequate | Insufficient |
|-----------|-----------|----------|--------------|
| Interpretation | Integrates evidence and limitations | Partial description | Erroneous interpretation |
| Visualization | Correct and clear | Partially adequate | Confusing |
| Inference | Avoids undue causality | Some imprecisions | Incorrect causal inference |

## Expected Responses
Students should identify that while variables are correlated, confounding factors (e.g., age, socioeconomic status) are not fully controlled.
